[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67462,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipomatous hamartoma of the atrioventricular valve (LHAV) is a benign valvular mass composed of unencapsulated mature adipocytes, small capillaries, and fibrous connective tissue.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67463,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "<p>None</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-18T12:13:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67464,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F01 Benign neoplasm of intrathoracic organs</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67465,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> primary valvular lipomatous hamartoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> cardiac valve lipomatosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67466,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67467,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "<p>As the name implies, these lesions are found in atrioventricular valves. Right-sided LHAVs are generally associated with the septal leaflet of the tricuspid valve, whereas LHAVs of both the anterior and posterior mitral valve leaflets have been observed {24821963}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T17:46:12"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67468,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Clinical features vary based on lesional location or may be entirely absent. In the few cases reported, flow murmurs with valvular insufficiency were the most common presenting findings {21036628}. Owing to their anatomical location, right-sided LHAVs have been associated with dyspnoea, whereas left-sided lesions may be associated with thromboembolic phenomena {24044592}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67469,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LHAV is exceedingly rare, with &lt;&nbsp;15&nbsp;reported cases in the literature. The lesion has been documented in a wide age range (2&ndash;76&nbsp;years). There is no sex predilection {21036628}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67470,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hamartomatous lesions, such as LHAV, are thought to be congenital in nature. There are no known genetic predispositions or associated causes.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67471,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although probably present at birth, the lesion may slowly enlarge (stretch) over time as the structurally dysplastic leaflet is subjected to ventricular systolic pressures {2013183}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67472,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The valve may appear thickened with a billowing contour, or it may show a nodular protuberance on either the ventricular or the atrial aspect of the leaflet {2013183; 21036628}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67473,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LHAV is composed of mature adipocytes admixed with mesenchymal elements native to the atrioventricular valve, such as fibroconnective tissue and thin-walled vasculature. Importantly, LHAV shows no features of fibrous encapsulation, distinguishing it from entities in the differential diagnosis, such as lipoma {24821963}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67474,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not described</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67475,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67476,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Unencapsulated collection of fat within the atrioventricular valve</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Grossly mass-forming</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67477,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67478,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although LHAV is histopathologically benign, it may have haemodynamic consequences secondary to its anatomical localization. Significant valvular regurgitation, premature ventricular contractions, presyncope, (thrombo)embolism, and sudden death have all been reported or are theoretical risks.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-01T09:40:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]